From e9bc1fbccae2e4f968105a401e35a9589b16c058 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:07:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ownership): defer update and unidentified lease owners
 without takeover [daveey]

Problem: ownership cards recurred during two observation windows
despite #3894, #3926 and #3930.

Why 1: the producer treated SESSION_NOT_OWNED as an actionable foreign
owner unless a narrow automatic-turn update-marker exception matched.
Evidence: prompt_turn._admit_prompt_turn; RED regressions for typed
update custody and opaque/PID-zero owners (red.log, eight failures).
Why 2: the durable refusal assigned lease_foreign without holder
identity. Its logged PID zero is missing telemetry, not proof that the
actual writer had no PID (session_lifecycle._durable_owner_refusal).
Why 3: no shared distinction separated a custody fence from positive
foreign-owner evidence for typed queue admission and automatic replay.
Root (happened): owner refusal classification also selected takeover UI;
a fail-closed refusal was incorrectly treated as takeover evidence.
Root (not caught): the watcher excluded every lease_foreign line, and
existing typed-update tests expected an error/card. Both encoded the
same invalid assumption, so the later incidents escaped detection.
Recurrence: #3894/#3926/#3930 addressed ledger/self-orphan/attested
update cases, not all typed and unidentified durable-holder paths.

Historical evidence boundary: both earlier card lines were
followed by automatic-turn refusals, not demonstrated typed entries.
A process served the same chat shortly beforehand and was its marker
writer; the available logs do not bind it to the earlier retirement.
In the later window a backend accepted auto_continue, held that chat's
marker and subsequently released its durable turn lease.
The competing PID-zero line cannot alone prove that exact
holder identity; no historical holder string was retained in that line.
Do not infer missing historical lease ownership from update timing.

Countermeasures:
- symptom: silent automatic deferral and durable typed queue/retry for
  attested updating/retiring or unidentified holders; no lease stealing.
- root: shared transient classification, verified PID/birth/install
  retirement evidence, positive remote evidence keeps foreign UI.
- retry: leave queued input intact while the owner fence still refuses.
- detection: add event-time holder_state to ownership-card logs; companion
  state watcher tests detect PID-zero and attested update/retirement
  foreign lines while excluding positive remote conflicts.
Proof: canonical six-file no-retry run: 206 passed; scripts/check: 21
checks OK. New queue integration retries twice before holder release.
Watcher RED: five failures; GREEN watcher/producer/installer: 72 passed.
Independent exact-head review, required CI and deployed 24h audit remain
landing/operational gates, not claims established by these local tests.
